# Rule D1's mutable-static half across modules: a Send global that one
# thread writes and another reads is a data race. `read_counter` (lib.yo) is
# judged from lib.yo's end-of-load summary, since `check` drops lib.yo's
# table when it finishes; `bump` writes `counter` (recorded by its
# definition-time trial and again by main's specialization). The spawned
# closure reaching `read_counter` must be rejected as `compile` rejects it —
# before the summary `check` said only "never evaluated"
# (issues/fixed/check-cannot-see-function-bodies-from-other-modules.md; the
# write-after-the-memo order is pinned by
# check-send-closure-reads-a-global-written-after-an-earlier-walk-rejected,
# issues/fixed/d1-thread-reach-misses-a-write-recorded-after-a-memoized-walk.md).
stdout_keep_match=global 'counter' [^,]*, which is assigned at
timeout=120
